1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:05,364
Meet Mochi. Emma and Alex share the care.

2
00:00:05,524 --> 00:00:09,820
Paw Twin brings their daily routine into one shared place.

3
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:17,578
Two sample weights, seven days apart, show a hundred fifty gram increase.

4
00:00:17,738 --> 00:00:24,098
The report keeps the calculation tied to its records, and missing food intake stays unknown.

5
00:00:25,250 --> 00:00:29,090
Mochi likes a feather toy and rests after meals.

6
00:00:29,250 --> 00:00:34,410
Emma confirms that preference before it becomes part of their shared pet context.

7
00:00:36,250 --> 00:00:40,786
Alex starts a fresh conversation in the Alexa web simulator.

8
00:00:40,946 --> 00:00:46,826
The next answer reads the same confirmed preference and makes its source available to inspect.

9
00:00:48,250 --> 00:00:51,634
Emma asks for playtime and chooses a time.

10
00:00:51,794 --> 00:00:56,570
The draft lets her review the plan before any care task exists.

11
00:00:57,333 --> 00:01:00,573
The prepared proposal is ready for review.

12
00:01:00,733 --> 00:01:03,877
It still needs an explicit confirmation.

13
00:01:05,333 --> 00:01:09,005
Emma confirms one shared manual care task.

14
00:01:09,165 --> 00:01:14,085
The result is clear: planned, and waiting for a person to complete it.

15
00:01:14,833 --> 00:01:19,081
Alex claims the task and records the playtime as completed.

16
00:01:19,241 --> 00:01:23,897
His account is attached to the record, so the handoff stays traceable.

17
00:01:26,833 --> 00:01:31,345
The household history identifies Alex and the completed care.

18
00:01:31,505 --> 00:01:34,529
Everyone can check the recorded result.

19
00:01:35,292 --> 00:01:40,020
Emma's daily report now counts one completed manual care task.

20
00:01:40,180 --> 00:01:44,596
It summarizes the saved records without inventing a health outcome.

21
00:01:45,375 --> 00:01:50,511
A helper can receive temporary, read-only access to one selected pet.

22
00:01:50,671 --> 00:01:53,023
The owner can revoke it.

23
00:01:53,792 --> 00:01:58,280
The visit card organizes dated records and shows what is missing.

24
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:02,376
It can be printed or saved for review with a veterinarian.

25
00:02:03,125 --> 00:02:07,589
When Emma deletes a preference, the next answer stops using it.

26
00:02:07,749 --> 00:02:12,045
A remembered fact is always subject to the owner's control.

27
00:02:13,125 --> 00:02:18,285
Paw Twin connects the pet's records, shared plans, and recorded care.

28
00:02:18,445 --> 00:02:28,381
This prototype uses local rules and SQLite. Alexa is a web simulation; live cloud and hardware integrations remain unverified.
